**/*.stories.tsx
**/e2e
# Transient lint fixtures the boundary/wiring/anti-slop suites write into a real
# `src` and delete again (genie-ops-center-v2-7lj). They are excluded from the
# lint, typecheck and unit collections; excluding them from the image context as
# well keeps a run that overlaps an image build from changing its context hash.
**/__boundary__*
**/__wiring__*
**/__antislop__*
# Generated by Next and git-ignored. `next build` and `next dev` write different
# contents, so a dev-server run between `build-image` and the image-freshness
# guard changed the context hash and failed the guard (genie-ops-center-v2-453).
# The build regenerates it.
**/next-env.d.ts
# Local environment files must not reach the build context: `next build` loads
# them and inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value into the client bundle that ships
# (genie-ops-center-v2-sl1). The example file stays, for a build that needs one.
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
